Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||07-10-2001||11:06 PM||||That must be their strip chip.<BR>I have one and I like it very much!<BR>You must remove the craptilitic perverter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>before installing this chip though.<BR>The ADS chips seem to work better for GM vehicles than the Hypertech's do.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000004||1FST2M6||07-11-2001||08:39 AM||||you don't have to remove the cat.. you will still pass emissions with the chip. i'd say save your $.. the HP gaines that i've seen don't warrant the $100+ get and MSD box, coil and a decent tune up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||07-11-2001||09:45 PM||||The strip chip is designed to work without the cat, that's why you have to remove it.<P>My chip did make a notable difference in performance. the Hypertech's don't do much.<BR>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
